1
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:45,640
Great work, guys.

2
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:47,320
- And sorry again.

3
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:49,880
I did not know it was their mating season.

4
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:51,560
Yes, Graham, my son! I've got it!

5
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:52,720
Got what?

6
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:54,800
The sixth coupon from the Bandohzi Herald.

7
00:00:54,840 --> 00:00:56,400
Keeps getting delivered by the coffee machine upstairs.

8
00:00:56,440 --> 00:00:57,440
Or is it downstairs?

9
00:00:57,480 --> 00:01:01,320
Anyway, don't matter. I noticed they had an offer on.

10
00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:03,960
Collect six coupons, get a free holiday.

11
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,280
I'm up for a free holiday.

12
00:01:05,320 --> 00:01:07,760
- Where is it? - A place called Tranquillity.

13
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:09,360
Me too. So long as there's plenty of sun

14
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:11,800
and absolutely no deep-space squid.

15
00:01:11,840 --> 00:01:13,280
Might get you out of your mardy mood.

16
00:01:14,320 --> 00:01:15,400
My mood's fine.

17
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:17,720
- That's you told.

18
00:01:17,760 --> 00:01:19,200
Hang on, Graham. They're not

19
00:01:19,240 --> 00:01:20,400
six perfect squares, are they?

20
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:22,200
No, don't put them together yet!

21
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:24,080
Bit late for that. - What's happening?

22
00:01:24,120 --> 00:01:26,120
I hope you've packed. They're not just coupons.

23
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:27,880
That's a teleport cube - just activated.

24
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:29,320
We've got about four seconds.

25
00:01:29,360 --> 00:01:31,280
No, no, no, no. I've got to go and fetch my Speedos.

26
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:35,280
Only joking. Already got 'em on. Ho-ho!

27
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:42,280
Welcome to Tranquillity Spa.

28
00:01:42,320 --> 00:01:44,920
Oh, guys! This is a bit of all right, innit?

29
00:01:44,960 --> 00:01:45,960
Welcome!

30
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,800
O'Brien party of four?

31
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:50,800
Bandohzi Herald coupons?

32
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:52,440
I'm Hyph3n with a 3,

33
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:55,760
your customer host here at Tranquillity Spa.

34
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:57,760
And relax!

35
00:01:57,800 --> 00:01:59,160
Hi, Hyph3n with a 3. Nice tail.

36
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:01,760
I'm a bit worried about being separated from my ship.

37
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:04,360
Our system has saved exactly where you came from.

38
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:06,880
You can return any time, but you're booked in for two weeks,

39
00:02:06,920 --> 00:02:08,320
all-inclusive.

40
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:09,360
Get in!

41
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:11,360
Your rooms are just being prepared.

42
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:12,800
Take a moment to explore

43
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:14,760
and I'll come and find you once they're ready.

44
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:16,240
I'm going to find the pool!

45
00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:18,000
I'm seeing what they've got inside the building.

46
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:21,200
And I am going to sit over there for three hours,

47
00:02:21,240 --> 00:02:24,240
then I'm going to get up and sit somewhere else,

48
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:26,200
and then cocktails. All-inclusive, Doc.

49
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:28,640
Got to get your coupons' worth. Get in!

50
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:30,920
Come on, Graham, son!

51
00:02:30,960 --> 00:02:32,880
I'll have a look round, then.

52
00:02:32,920 --> 00:02:34,600
By myself.

53
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:45,240
Relax. Our staff are being informed.

54
00:02:47,320 --> 00:02:48,760
- Another system virus. - Vorm, I don't care.

55
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:50,160
We've got a physical breach.

56
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:51,600
One of them's got in.

57
00:02:51,640 --> 00:02:54,520
Find it, contain it, and radio in.

58
00:02:54,560 --> 00:02:55,560
Do not engage without me.

59
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:05,800
Look at that, Vilma. Can you believe it?

60
00:03:05,840 --> 00:03:08,520
Oh, it's perfect, Benni.

61
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:10,160
Thank you.

62
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:13,440
I saw some newlyweds up at reception.

63
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:15,400
Nice place to come for a honeymoon.

64
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:18,160
We've had 46 years.

65
00:03:18,200 --> 00:03:19,960
We never needed to be married.

66
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:22,000
You say that...

67
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:23,080
...but...

68
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:24,440
Wow!

69
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:27,360
Oh, hello. Not bad, is it?

70
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:29,000
It's absolutely gorgeous.

71
00:03:29,040 --> 00:03:30,160
Um...

72
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:31,520
This place has got everything.

73
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:37,280
Welcome to Tranquillity's bar and refreshment zone.

74
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:40,040
We serve all your favourites, all-inclusive.

75
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:41,520
Oh, free stuff!

76
00:03:44,640 --> 00:03:46,040
- Ooh

77
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:47,840
- Ow! Ow!

78
00:03:47,880 --> 00:03:49,320
Fighting with the vending machine?

79
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:51,000
No, it just gave me an electric shock.

80
00:03:51,040 --> 00:03:52,560
That's not a shock.

81
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:54,120
It's a hopper virus.

82
00:03:54,160 --> 00:03:54,960
This machine's sick,

83
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,440
and it just passed its virus on to you.

84
00:03:56,480 --> 00:03:58,200
How did I get a virus the same as a vending machine?

85
00:03:58,240 --> 00:03:59,280
I'm not a machine.

86
00:03:59,320 --> 00:04:01,440
Hoppers are multi-platform. They'll go for anything.

87
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:03,280
- Don't pick at it! - Did it just go through me?

88
00:04:03,320 --> 00:04:04,320
It's moving deeper inside you

89
00:04:04,360 --> 00:04:05,640
to mutate into your nervous system.

90
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:06,680
What?

91
00:04:06,720 --> 00:04:07,800
Important not to panic.

92
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:09,760
Humans always have the same reaction to a hopper virus.

93
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:11,080
First you get the wiggly fingers,

94
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:12,840
which is a warning the legs are about to go.

95
00:04:12,880 --> 00:04:13,680
Luckily,

96
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:15,560
this is where my hopper first-aid training kicks in.

97
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:19,200
Need to get rid of these.

98
00:04:19,240 --> 00:04:21,360
Then pinch your ear.

99
00:04:21,400 --> 00:04:23,360
- Then you're going to sneeze. - Atchoo!

100
00:04:23,400 --> 00:04:27,440
Yes! Now suck your thumb until the hallucinations stop.

101
00:04:27,480 --> 00:04:30,360
And remember, they're not real bats.

102
00:04:30,400 --> 00:04:32,680
- He's fine.

103
00:04:32,720 --> 00:04:34,320
He's fine.

104
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,160
Make the bats go away!

105
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:38,440
Hotel perimeter breach.

106
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:40,560
Initiating guest protection measures.

107
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:41,800
It's on the move again, Vorm.

108
00:04:41,840 --> 00:04:43,960
Be careful.

109
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:46,120
I'm Vilma. Nice to meet you.

110
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:47,560
This is Benni.

111
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:49,840
Yaz. Just arrived.

112
00:04:49,880 --> 00:04:50,960
Sorry, I didn't mean to interrupt.

113
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,120
- Oh, you're all right... - Well, you were a bit...

114
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:55,840
All guests, please assemble at your nearest muster station.

115
00:04:55,880 --> 00:04:57,600
Relax.

116
00:04:57,640 --> 00:05:00,520
This is a routine Tranquillity drill.

117
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:03,760
All guests, please assemble at your nearest muster station.

118
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:05,920
If this is anything to do with you, Doc...

119
00:05:05,960 --> 00:05:07,000
Relax.

120
00:05:07,040 --> 00:05:08,520
This is a routine Tranquillity drill.

121
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:11,160
Stay here. I'll investigate. It's probably nothing.

122
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:12,840
Usually nothing.

123
00:05:12,880 --> 00:05:14,640
I say "usually"...

124
00:05:14,680 --> 00:05:19,360
All guests, please assemble at your nearest muster station.

125
00:05:19,400 --> 00:05:23,840
The nearest muster station to this zone is the teleport pad.

126
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:27,960
Hopper virus got you too?

127
00:05:29,240 --> 00:05:31,520
I'm not sure about this place.

128
00:05:33,360 --> 00:05:34,760
So...

129
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:37,120
...you here with family?

130
00:05:40,120 --> 00:05:41,560
Hotel critic.

131
00:05:41,600 --> 00:05:43,240
Mm.

132
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:44,320
You?

133
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:47,800
Oh, I'm here with my mates, yeah.

134
00:05:47,840 --> 00:05:50,160
I'm a pilot...surgeon... pilot...surgeon...

135
00:05:50,200 --> 00:05:52,200
I'm a surgeon for pilots.

136
00:05:52,240 --> 00:05:56,360
So, do you come across many hopper viruses?

137
00:05:56,400 --> 00:05:58,040
Does this usually work?

138
00:05:58,080 --> 00:05:59,600
- What? - Pretending to be stupid

139
00:05:59,640 --> 00:06:01,080
so girls have to answer your questions?

140
00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:03,560
Hey, look, I'm not trying to chat you up.

141
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:07,760
Shame.

142
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:12,080
I'm Bella.

143
00:06:13,400 --> 00:06:14,480
Oh...

144
00:06:14,520 --> 00:06:15,760
Heading to the east zone.

145
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:17,160
I'll isolate it there.

146
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:22,600
If this is a drill, what's he doing with a gun?

147
00:06:24,880 --> 00:06:26,560
Do you want to find out?

148
00:06:28,160 --> 00:06:31,320
Relax. This is a routine Tranquillity drill.

149
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:32,800
Coming up to linen cupboard now.

150
00:06:32,840 --> 00:06:34,520
Hyph3n with a 3!

151
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:36,880
I just pulled this out of a friend of mine.

152
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:39,440
Well, we do not make any judgments on our guests

153
00:06:39,480 --> 00:06:41,720
and fully support any way you choose to enjoy yourself

154
00:06:41,760 --> 00:06:42,880
here at Tranquillity Spa.

155
00:06:42,920 --> 00:06:45,240
It wasn't recreational. This is a weapon.

156
00:06:45,280 --> 00:06:46,920
I'd say someone is targeting you.

157
00:06:46,960 --> 00:06:48,160
Now, why would they do that?

158
00:06:48,200 --> 00:06:50,280
Also, why is that alarm going off?

159
00:06:50,320 --> 00:06:51,480
And why do you look so concerned?

160
00:06:51,520 --> 00:06:53,080
Also, where does the 3 come in "Hyphen"?

161
00:06:53,120 --> 00:06:54,800
Never mind. That one can wait.

162
00:06:54,840 --> 00:06:57,360
Also... Also, what's behind that door?

163
00:06:57,400 --> 00:06:58,920
Cos no linen cupboard needs a key

164
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:00,640
with that many security gradings.

165
00:07:00,680 --> 00:07:01,680
I want to take a look.

166
00:07:01,720 --> 00:07:04,480
Guests aren't permitted in the...linen cupboard.

167
00:07:04,520 --> 00:07:06,160
How about...

168
00:07:06,200 --> 00:07:09,040
...Pan-galactic Standards and Practices Officer?

169
00:07:09,080 --> 00:07:10,720
Health and Safety?

170
00:07:10,760 --> 00:07:13,080
Security and Hygiene?

171
00:07:13,120 --> 00:07:14,240
Resort Inspector?

172
00:07:14,280 --> 00:07:16,920
Now, are you and your excellent tail

173
00:07:16,960 --> 00:07:18,240
going to let me have a look,

174
00:07:18,280 --> 00:07:20,840
or am I going to have to bark at you? Cos I will.

175
00:07:24,280 --> 00:07:26,120
It's after the second H and before the final N.

176
00:07:26,160 --> 00:07:28,000
- The 3. - Oh, yeah!

177
00:07:28,040 --> 00:07:29,320
Course.

178
00:07:32,480 --> 00:07:35,320
Deadlocked room with its own armoury.

179
00:07:35,360 --> 00:07:38,040
Don't tell me. Honeymoon suite?

180
00:07:38,080 --> 00:07:39,840
Hyph3n, what the hell are you doing?

181
00:07:39,880 --> 00:07:40,760
Who's this?

182
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:43,520
I'm the Doctor, and you, madam, are far too handsy.

183
00:07:43,560 --> 00:07:44,640
Resort Inspector.

184
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:46,160
We've only just been inspected.

185
00:07:46,200 --> 00:07:48,520
Well, we like to surprise. Just like this hopper virus

186
00:07:48,560 --> 00:07:49,920
I found in your vending machine.

187
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:52,760
This will mutate any system it hops into and wreck it.

188
00:07:52,800 --> 00:07:54,120
This is part of a family set,

189
00:07:54,160 --> 00:07:57,240
so there are other replications out there, which might explain

190
00:07:57,280 --> 00:07:59,200
why your ionic membrane's failed.

191
00:08:00,880 --> 00:08:02,800
Why would you need to defend a holiday spa

192
00:08:02,840 --> 00:08:05,240
with an ionic membrane?

193
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:09,120
Power systems in this zone of Tranquillity

194
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:10,800
are currently experiencing challenges.

195
00:08:16,280 --> 00:08:17,760
Help me!

196
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:20,240
- Relax, and leave immediately. - Please!

197
00:08:20,280 --> 00:08:21,960
- Please! - Confirmed sighting.

198
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:23,480
It's on the loose inside.

199
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,000
It's attacking the guests.

200
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:30,320
What did he say? What's attacking the guests?

201
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:32,000
Why do you need all this? Tell me.

202
00:08:32,040 --> 00:08:33,560
Do not engage. I'm en route.

203
00:08:33,600 --> 00:08:35,520
We have to implement teleport evacuation procedures.

204
00:08:35,560 --> 00:08:36,960
Don't tell me about the procedures, Hyph3n.

205
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:38,000
I wrote them.

206
00:08:38,040 --> 00:08:39,560
You can forget about evacuation.

207
00:08:39,600 --> 00:08:41,720
The hopper virus is in your teleport system.

208
00:08:41,760 --> 00:08:42,720
Everything's down.

209
00:08:42,760 --> 00:08:44,880
I need you here to help me understand this place,

210
00:08:44,920 --> 00:08:47,480
not out there shooting at things.

211
00:08:49,520 --> 00:08:51,600
This zone of Tranquillity is compromised.

212
00:08:51,640 --> 00:08:55,480
If you can hear this message, you shouldn't be here.

213
00:08:55,520 --> 00:08:57,240
Leave immediately.

214
00:08:57,280 --> 00:08:59,320
- Stay back!

215
00:09:07,200 --> 00:09:10,000
Kane, there's more than one. I have to retreat!

216
00:09:12,640 --> 00:09:14,680
Something's down there. In here.

217
00:09:15,800 --> 00:09:17,480
Good, here we go. You're maintenance, right?

218
00:09:17,520 --> 00:09:18,720
You're just the fella.

219
00:09:18,760 --> 00:09:21,640
You are needed outside.

220
00:09:21,680 --> 00:09:22,920
Some of the guests reckon that

221
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:24,240
the teleport on the terrace ain't working.

222
00:09:24,280 --> 00:09:27,080
Yeah, nothing's working, mate, sorry.

223
00:09:27,120 --> 00:09:29,000
Where's my snap hammer?

224
00:09:29,040 --> 00:09:30,960
Sylas?

225
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:33,880
Snap hammer won't fix that. You want a crash wrench.

226
00:09:33,920 --> 00:09:36,960
Oi, you're not a mechanic. You're a child.

227
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:38,600
Now pass me the snap hammer.

228
00:09:38,640 --> 00:09:41,120
I'm Nevi. This is my boy Sylas.

229
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:42,200
All right, Sylas?

230
00:09:42,240 --> 00:09:43,960
Yeah, he likes to show up without warning.

231
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,040
This place is way better than Mum's house.

232
00:09:46,080 --> 00:09:48,640
How many people have you got staying here?

233
00:09:48,680 --> 00:09:51,200
23. This shows all their positions.

234
00:09:51,240 --> 00:09:52,760
- Guest offline. - No, 21 now.

235
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:55,320
Guest online. Guest off...

236
00:09:56,640 --> 00:09:58,360
- 19. - ...offline.

237
00:09:58,400 --> 00:10:00,320
Guest offline. Guest offline.

238
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:01,960
Our friends are out there.

239
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:04,600
All guests within the hotel building,

240
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:07,480
to the linen cupboard in the north corridor immediately.

241
00:10:07,520 --> 00:10:08,600
It's just a drill.

242
00:10:08,640 --> 00:10:10,720
Not a drill.

243
00:10:10,760 --> 00:10:12,040
Repeat, not a drill.

244
00:10:12,080 --> 00:10:14,440
I'm sure it's nothing to worry about.

245
00:10:19,920 --> 00:10:22,640
We should probably head to the linen cupboard.

246
00:10:22,680 --> 00:10:24,120
Guest offline.

247
00:10:24,160 --> 00:10:26,320
Where's your security team?

248
00:10:26,360 --> 00:10:28,080
No team. Just me and Vorm.

249
00:10:29,080 --> 00:10:32,400
This zone of Tranquillity is compromised.

250
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:35,000
Please do not enter the Tranquillity steam room

251
00:10:35,040 --> 00:10:36,680
during this routine drill.

252
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:38,360
Help! Please, it's coming!

253
00:10:38,400 --> 00:10:39,920
Hey, what's out there? - It's seen me!

254
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:41,880
- What...? Shut up!

255
00:10:41,920 --> 00:10:43,800
Welcome to the Tranquillity steam room.

256
00:10:43,840 --> 00:10:45,600
Please leave immediately.

257
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:49,320
Hey.

258
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:51,800
- I'm not a surgeon for pilots.

259
00:10:51,840 --> 00:10:53,520
I work in a warehouse.

260
00:10:53,560 --> 00:10:55,160
I'm not a hotel critic.

261
00:10:55,200 --> 00:10:57,720
I just... I didn't want to say "unemployed nobody".

262
00:11:00,400 --> 00:11:04,600
An unauthorised life form has entered the steam room.

263
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:08,520
This debug script should neutralise the hopper viruses,

264
00:11:08,560 --> 00:11:09,840
but they'll need time to work.

265
00:11:09,880 --> 00:11:13,360
More urgently, I need to build a new ionic membrane

266
00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:15,200
to banish whatever is killing your guests.

267
00:11:15,240 --> 00:11:17,640
You can't build an ionic membrane from scratch.

268
00:11:17,680 --> 00:11:19,200
If I had crayons and half a can of Spam,

269
00:11:19,240 --> 00:11:21,280
I could build you from scratch. Now, out of my way.

270
00:11:24,840 --> 00:11:26,720
They'll take the bodies, won't they?

271
00:11:26,760 --> 00:11:29,680
There you are. We heard the Doctor's voice over the Tannoy.

272
00:11:29,720 --> 00:11:31,840
Also gunfire. And people screaming.

273
00:11:31,880 --> 00:11:33,520
Yeah, I know. I've been on better holidays.

274
00:11:33,560 --> 00:11:35,880
All of you, in here.

275
00:11:38,520 --> 00:11:40,200
That's a funny kind of linen cupboard.

276
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:41,840
Hi, can't talk. Building.

277
00:11:43,640 --> 00:11:45,440
Always the hat, Vilma.

278
00:11:50,400 --> 00:11:52,920
I'm losing visuals across the compound.

279
00:11:52,960 --> 00:11:55,200
I don't know how many of those creatures have got in.

280
00:11:55,240 --> 00:11:57,680
Kane, I'm sorry. I couldn't stop it.

281
00:11:57,720 --> 00:11:59,680
It's your job to stop it, Vorm.

282
00:12:02,480 --> 00:12:06,080
Those things are heading for the guest teleport.

283
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:09,640
Benni, I dropped my hat.

284
00:12:12,360 --> 00:12:14,240
Where's Benni?

285
00:12:14,280 --> 00:12:16,280
And where's Ryan?

286
00:12:18,960 --> 00:12:20,080
Shh!

287
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:22,440
Don't run.

288
00:12:22,480 --> 00:12:24,160
Psst.

289
00:12:28,200 --> 00:12:29,520
I got it.

290
00:12:29,560 --> 00:12:31,000
Ionic membrane.

291
00:12:31,040 --> 00:12:32,880
Reinstated DNA filter.

292
00:12:32,920 --> 00:12:35,200
It'll exile any life form not pre-approved.

293
00:12:35,240 --> 00:12:36,760
If I've built this right.

294
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:06,560
Yes. It worked!

295
00:13:06,600 --> 00:13:08,000
Seal is secure.

296
00:13:08,040 --> 00:13:11,480
Internal O2 level restored to 20.5%.

297
00:13:11,520 --> 00:13:13,400
The ionic membrane's forced those things out.

298
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:18,080
Now open the door. Our friend's out there.

299
00:13:18,120 --> 00:13:19,760
What are those red dots?

300
00:13:19,800 --> 00:13:21,840
Casualties of the Dregs. Don't look, Sylas.

301
00:13:23,680 --> 00:13:25,520
Has it gone?

302
00:13:27,080 --> 00:13:28,240
What just happened?

303
00:13:29,840 --> 00:13:31,520
If I had to guess...

304
00:13:31,560 --> 00:13:32,880
...The Doctor.

305
00:13:35,240 --> 00:13:37,320
Can you show me Ryan? Where's Ryan on there?

306
00:13:37,360 --> 00:13:38,640
I'm so sorry.

307
00:13:45,880 --> 00:13:49,160
Yaz, I can't see Benni on there either.

308
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:51,240
Where's Benni?

309
00:13:52,880 --> 00:13:54,640
Ryan!

310
00:13:54,680 --> 00:13:56,280
Ryan!

311
00:13:57,840 --> 00:14:00,200
Ryan! Ryan!

312
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:01,520
- Graham. - Oh!

313
00:14:01,560 --> 00:14:03,440
What's happening?

314
00:14:03,480 --> 00:14:05,120
Oh, Ryan!

315
00:14:05,160 --> 00:14:07,160
It ain't the aliens that are gonna kill me,

316
00:14:07,200 --> 00:14:08,600
it's worrying about you.

317
00:14:10,160 --> 00:14:12,360
What is it that got in here?

318
00:14:12,400 --> 00:14:13,880
A couple of the locals. Dregs.

319
00:14:13,920 --> 00:14:15,360
They're always trying to attack.

320
00:14:15,400 --> 00:14:16,600
That's why we have shields.

321
00:14:16,640 --> 00:14:18,440
But the virus that brought the shields down,

322
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:20,000
the Dregs couldn't have done that.

323
00:14:20,040 --> 00:14:21,320
Somebody hacked the system.

324
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:22,880
Who'd sabotage a hotel?

325
00:14:22,920 --> 00:14:25,560
Vorm, void panel SE9-13.

326
00:14:33,960 --> 00:14:35,520
What is happening right now?

327
00:14:35,560 --> 00:14:36,880
Ooh.

328
00:14:36,920 --> 00:14:39,800
Cor blimey! Right on me nut!

329
00:14:39,840 --> 00:14:41,560
Am I having a stroke or something?

330
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:43,040
- It's a fake-cation. A what?

331
00:14:43,080 --> 00:14:44,200
A really good one.

332
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:46,240
What? So none of this is real?

333
00:14:46,280 --> 00:14:49,160
The hotel is, and the pool.

334
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:51,240
But you reach a certain point...

335
00:14:52,280 --> 00:14:56,360
These are usually built in cities so no-one has to travel.

336
00:14:56,400 --> 00:14:58,080
Our guests now get off-world holiday

337
00:14:58,120 --> 00:14:59,160
for a fraction of the price.

338
00:14:59,200 --> 00:15:00,960
If they survive.

339
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,840
You built this somewhere you shouldn't,

340
00:15:02,880 --> 00:15:04,040
thinking no-one'd notice

341
00:15:04,080 --> 00:15:06,680
if you could only get in and out by teleport.

342
00:15:06,720 --> 00:15:08,760
I heard your little chat about O2 levels.

343
00:15:08,800 --> 00:15:10,200
That's a completely different environment

344
00:15:10,240 --> 00:15:11,640
out there. The native species

345
00:15:11,680 --> 00:15:13,600
want you and your guests dead.

346
00:15:13,640 --> 00:15:16,120
Doctor, you need to see this!

347
00:15:16,160 --> 00:15:18,240
They've built a wall all around this hotel.

348
00:15:18,280 --> 00:15:20,680
Vilma said it's the first off-world fake-cation.

349
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:23,760
Done that bit. Feel the lump on my bonce. Do that.

350
00:15:23,800 --> 00:15:26,400
- What? - But my Benni is missing.

351
00:15:26,440 --> 00:15:28,520
According to this, he's outside the shields.

352
00:15:28,560 --> 00:15:31,160
You can't just walk outside. There's not enough oxygen.

353
00:15:31,200 --> 00:15:32,440
He'd be dead before we reach him.

354
00:15:32,480 --> 00:15:34,960
He has an oxygen tank.

355
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:37,400
We have to find him.

356
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:38,600
He came here because of you.

357
00:15:40,120 --> 00:15:42,160
If there's even the slightest chance of finding him,

358
00:15:42,200 --> 00:15:43,920
you need to do it. We'll help.

359
00:15:43,960 --> 00:15:46,960
Get transport. I'll gather everyone in the bar.

360
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:51,320
Now, Kane!

361
00:15:57,480 --> 00:16:01,080
You get one O2 canister each. Conserve it.

362
00:16:01,120 --> 00:16:03,800
Green is good, orange is bad, red's dead.

363
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:05,080
Oh...

364
00:16:05,120 --> 00:16:06,840
The good news - these are smart.

365
00:16:06,880 --> 00:16:09,080
In an O2-rich environment, they refill themselves.

366
00:16:09,120 --> 00:16:11,120
Outside this dome, the only O2-rich environment

367
00:16:11,160 --> 00:16:13,320
on the planet will be inside the truck.

368
00:16:13,360 --> 00:16:15,720
Do not exit without my permission.

369
00:16:15,760 --> 00:16:17,840
Keep an eye on your readings.

370
00:16:17,880 --> 00:16:20,800
They'll change colour if you are running low on oxygen.

371
00:16:20,840 --> 00:16:25,120
Nevi, cockle, my nose thingy and this breathing apparatus,

372
00:16:25,160 --> 00:16:26,160
is it on right?

373
00:16:26,200 --> 00:16:27,240
Yeah, it's fine.

374
00:16:27,280 --> 00:16:28,800
Dad, it-it's not right.

375
00:16:30,040 --> 00:16:31,520
We'd better go and fire up the truck.

376
00:16:31,560 --> 00:16:33,280
Yeah. - I built it myself.

377
00:16:33,320 --> 00:16:34,360
Good.

378
00:16:34,400 --> 00:16:36,600
Tell me you helped him build it.

379
00:16:36,640 --> 00:16:37,800
We're moving out!

380
00:16:40,160 --> 00:16:41,520
You owe me some answers.

381
00:16:41,560 --> 00:16:42,840
This is my operation.

382
00:16:42,880 --> 00:16:44,840
Well, it's clearly going well. What planet is this?

383
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:46,240
Orphan 55.

384
00:16:46,280 --> 00:16:49,200
You built a fake-cation on an orphan planet? Are you mad?

385
00:16:49,240 --> 00:16:51,720
The radiation's dropped. It's safe in short spells.

386
00:16:51,760 --> 00:16:53,200
Get in the truck.

387
00:16:56,960 --> 00:16:59,800
Always remain inside the vehicle.

388
00:16:59,840 --> 00:17:02,960
This vehicle is the property of Tranquillity Spa,

389
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:05,120
your home from home.

390
00:17:09,360 --> 00:17:10,920
Was we inside that?

391
00:17:10,960 --> 00:17:12,640
This whole planet looks dead.

392
00:17:12,680 --> 00:17:15,720
It is. It's an orphan planet.

393
00:17:15,760 --> 00:17:18,760
It's a grading that means it's become too toxic for life.

394
00:17:18,800 --> 00:17:20,000
We're not safe out here.

395
00:17:20,040 --> 00:17:23,000
Well, we weren't exactly safe in there.

396
00:17:28,720 --> 00:17:32,040
Come on, Doc, explain. Why is it called an orphan planet?

397
00:17:32,080 --> 00:17:34,320
Because it's uninhabitable. In societies

398
00:17:34,360 --> 00:17:36,960
that let this happen, there's nearly always a ruling elite

399
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:39,920
that gets to evacuate, and then signs off all responsibility

400
00:17:39,960 --> 00:17:41,680
for whatever they've left behind.

401
00:17:41,720 --> 00:17:42,760
That's messed up.

402
00:17:42,800 --> 00:17:44,320
Happens more than you think.

403
00:17:44,360 --> 00:17:46,240
This is Orphan 55.

404
00:17:46,280 --> 00:17:47,880
And if you can't evacuate?

405
00:17:47,920 --> 00:17:51,680
You die. All sentient life dies.

406
00:17:51,720 --> 00:17:53,200
That's how it gets the grading.

407
00:17:53,240 --> 00:17:56,200
Except on Orphan 55, something clearly survived.

408
00:17:56,240 --> 00:17:57,440
The Dregs.

409
00:17:57,480 --> 00:18:00,360
Why here, Kane? Why build this hotel?

410
00:18:00,400 --> 00:18:01,840
It doesn't make any sense.

411
00:18:01,880 --> 00:18:03,040
The air's unbreathable,

412
00:18:03,080 --> 00:18:04,880
but a few years with the right terraforming,

413
00:18:04,920 --> 00:18:07,000
we can reduce the CO2 and make the whole planet habitable.

414
00:18:07,040 --> 00:18:10,120
Terraforming bankrolled by fake-cation.

415
00:18:10,160 --> 00:18:11,440
Smart.

416
00:18:11,480 --> 00:18:13,000
Today hotelier, tomorrow...

417
00:18:13,040 --> 00:18:15,720
...the proud owner of Orphan 55,

418
00:18:15,760 --> 00:18:17,960
the best real estate in the galaxy.

419
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:20,400
If you can sort out your Dreg problem, you'll be rich.

420
00:18:22,200 --> 00:18:25,120
Hey, Doc. Benni's changed direction.

421
00:18:25,160 --> 00:18:27,680
Why would he do that?

422
00:18:30,560 --> 00:18:32,920
Maybe he's heading back to the dome.

423
00:18:34,640 --> 00:18:36,960
- Abort the mission.

424
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:38,640
He's alive! We know where he is!

425
00:18:38,680 --> 00:18:41,640
He's moving at 37 clicks an hour.

426
00:18:41,680 --> 00:18:43,600
That doesn't sound like my Benni.

427
00:18:43,640 --> 00:18:45,440
The Dregs got him. We abort.

428
00:18:45,480 --> 00:18:50,600
If those things have got Benni, we're getting him back!

429
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:53,680
You want money, Kane? That's worth a fortune!

430
00:18:53,720 --> 00:18:55,200
That would buy a lot of terraforming.

431
00:18:55,240 --> 00:18:58,000
Or don't you want to be Queen of Orphan 55 any more, Kane?

432
00:18:58,040 --> 00:19:00,960
Never mind the money, there's a man's life at stake.

433
00:19:07,240 --> 00:19:09,080
Vorm, follow the tracker.

434
00:19:09,120 --> 00:19:10,600
- Oh...

435
00:19:14,240 --> 00:19:17,720
External oxygen levels - 2%.

436
00:19:17,760 --> 00:19:21,320
Current internal oxygen levels - 21%.

437
00:19:21,360 --> 00:19:22,680
Always remain in...

438
00:19:22,720 --> 00:19:25,000
So what do you actually know about the Dregs?

439
00:19:25,040 --> 00:19:26,680
How many are there?

440
00:19:26,720 --> 00:19:28,640
...is the property of Tranquillity Spa.

441
00:19:30,080 --> 00:19:32,280
Don't want to talk to me? Fine.

442
00:19:32,320 --> 00:19:33,760
I don't need a second person for a conversation.

443
00:19:33,800 --> 00:19:36,480
A lot of the time they just get in the way. So...

444
00:19:36,520 --> 00:19:39,800
A Dreg is a native species that somehow lived

445
00:19:39,840 --> 00:19:41,760
through the fallout.

446
00:19:41,800 --> 00:19:44,640
That's generations. There must be a few of them.

447
00:19:44,680 --> 00:19:47,280
Hyph3n with a 3, your face tells me I'm right.

448
00:19:47,320 --> 00:19:49,000
But how did they survive?

449
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:53,920
And why is your gun fitted with an exciplex modulator?

450
00:19:53,960 --> 00:19:55,920
They randomise laser output.

451
00:19:57,280 --> 00:19:59,080
You'd only need that against a thing

452
00:19:59,120 --> 00:20:00,800
that could adapt to your attack.

453
00:20:02,560 --> 00:20:03,920
Hang on.

454
00:20:05,680 --> 00:20:07,360
That's what they do?

455
00:20:07,400 --> 00:20:08,880
Adapt?

456
00:20:08,920 --> 00:20:11,760
To guns and to nuclear winter?!

457
00:20:11,800 --> 00:20:14,440
Apex predators! And we... We are driving

458
00:20:14,480 --> 00:20:16,400
straight into their territory!

459
00:20:37,320 --> 00:20:38,840
So, er...

460
00:20:41,920 --> 00:20:44,480
...how long have you been unemployed?

461
00:20:45,760 --> 00:20:48,000
Is that the worst chat-up line ever?

462
00:20:49,720 --> 00:20:51,240
Yeah.

463
00:20:51,280 --> 00:20:53,000
You just witnessed history.

464
00:20:58,960 --> 00:21:01,920
I've been unemployed for a month.

465
00:21:01,960 --> 00:21:04,920
I was my dad's carer, but...he died.

466
00:21:06,080 --> 00:21:07,960
Oh. Sorry.

467
00:21:09,480 --> 00:21:11,560
I lost my mum eight years back.

468
00:21:12,880 --> 00:21:16,080
Have you got anyone else? Is your mum around?

469
00:21:16,120 --> 00:21:18,880
She died when I was about Sylas's age.

470
00:21:18,920 --> 00:21:21,160
She made Nevi look like Parent of the Year.

471
00:21:22,680 --> 00:21:25,440
So...guys...

472
00:21:25,480 --> 00:21:27,360
...what's going on?

473
00:21:29,400 --> 00:21:31,080
Just talking.

474
00:21:31,120 --> 00:21:33,040
- Having a conversation. - Great.

475
00:21:33,080 --> 00:21:35,120
Where are we up to?

476
00:21:35,160 --> 00:21:38,720
Yeah, Ryan. What are you talking about?

477
00:21:40,280 --> 00:21:43,760
Er, er, we both have dead parents.

478
00:21:45,320 --> 00:21:48,000
This vehicle is experiencing momentary difficulties.

479
00:21:48,040 --> 00:21:51,800
This vehicle is experiencing momentary difficulties.

480
00:21:54,360 --> 00:21:56,520
This vehicle is compromised.

481
00:21:56,560 --> 00:21:58,560
What the hell was that?

482
00:21:58,600 --> 00:22:01,960
This vehicle is compromised.

483
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:05,480
Please stay inside the vehicle and wait for assistance.

484
00:22:05,520 --> 00:22:07,760
This is a trap, presumably set by the Dregs.

485
00:22:07,800 --> 00:22:09,560
This mist is highly toxic,

486
00:22:09,600 --> 00:22:11,720
and when it clears, direct sunlight is worse.

487
00:22:11,760 --> 00:22:14,600
We get ten minutes of solar blistering and then...

488
00:22:14,640 --> 00:22:15,920
...death.

489
00:22:17,600 --> 00:22:19,520
Solar blistering? What a lovely phrase.

490
00:22:19,560 --> 00:22:20,600
Here's another one.

491
00:22:20,640 --> 00:22:23,240
Completely knackered vehicle. We're stranded.

492
00:22:23,280 --> 00:22:24,880
I need to check where we are.

493
00:22:28,200 --> 00:22:30,320
There's a service tunnel close by.

494
00:22:30,360 --> 00:22:33,480
If we can make it to that, we might live.

495
00:22:33,520 --> 00:22:35,520
OK. Bad news is, we have to leave the truck

496
00:22:35,560 --> 00:22:36,560
and head out on foot.

497
00:22:36,600 --> 00:22:39,520
Not ideal, but basically our only option.

498
00:22:39,560 --> 00:22:41,640
We can't leave! I paid you.

499
00:22:41,680 --> 00:22:43,520
We came here for Benni!

500
00:22:43,560 --> 00:22:45,160
Stay quiet, move fast.

501
00:22:45,200 --> 00:22:46,880
Kane! Kane!

502
00:22:46,920 --> 00:22:47,960
All right, let's go.

503
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:49,640
We'll find him, Vilma, I promise.

504
00:22:56,720 --> 00:22:59,640
Tunnel entrance is just past this ridge.

505
00:23:04,160 --> 00:23:06,800
Benni! Benni! Where are you?

506
00:23:06,840 --> 00:23:08,120
- Shh, shh! - Oh...

507
00:23:08,160 --> 00:23:09,280
You'll bring the Dregs.

508
00:23:09,320 --> 00:23:12,400
They're massing in the hills all around us.

509
00:23:16,760 --> 00:23:18,400
Doc, we don't stand a chance.

510
00:23:26,480 --> 00:23:29,440
Everyone, back to the truck! Now!

511
00:23:29,480 --> 00:23:30,800
Go, go!

512
00:23:36,440 --> 00:23:37,560
So what's the plan now?

513
00:23:37,600 --> 00:23:39,120
Shut...up.

514
00:23:51,560 --> 00:23:52,520
What are we going to do?

515
00:23:52,560 --> 00:23:54,440
Vorm, we're going to deal with the Dregs.

516
00:23:54,480 --> 00:23:58,160
Doctor, get them out, head east, look for a hatch.

517
00:23:58,200 --> 00:23:59,400
We'll keep them busy.

518
00:24:01,440 --> 00:24:02,960
Vilma.

519
00:24:05,680 --> 00:24:07,120
Are you in there?

520
00:24:07,160 --> 00:24:09,120
Benni?

521
00:24:09,160 --> 00:24:11,360
- Benni! - Shh!

522
00:24:11,400 --> 00:24:14,040
- Benni! - Shh-shh.

523
00:24:14,080 --> 00:24:15,280
The Dregs have got him.

524
00:24:15,320 --> 00:24:16,840
Shh-shh-shh.

525
00:24:16,880 --> 00:24:19,320
Vilma!

526
00:24:19,360 --> 00:24:21,880
I can't believe you came!

527
00:24:21,920 --> 00:24:25,000
I'm not alone, and I don't have long...

528
00:24:26,360 --> 00:24:29,520
...but I-I have two questions.

529
00:24:29,560 --> 00:24:31,920
I'm sorry to ask them together.

530
00:24:33,400 --> 00:24:35,000
Will you marry me?

531
00:24:35,040 --> 00:24:38,920
Oh, of course I will!

532
00:24:38,960 --> 00:24:41,520
Yes!

533
00:24:41,560 --> 00:24:43,280
What was the other one?

534
00:24:43,320 --> 00:24:44,400
If anyone can,

535
00:24:44,440 --> 00:24:46,520
will they please shoot me?

536
00:24:46,560 --> 00:24:49,600
- Oh, Benni!

537
00:24:49,640 --> 00:24:52,080
What has it done to you?

538
00:24:54,920 --> 00:24:56,640
We've got to get out of here.

539
00:24:56,680 --> 00:24:59,280
We shouldn't have left the dome.

540
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:03,840
Vorm! This is it!

541
00:25:03,880 --> 00:25:05,520
- This is the job! Come on!

542
00:25:08,400 --> 00:25:09,960
Let's go!

543
00:25:10,000 --> 00:25:12,520
Sylas, now! Head to the ridge. Don't look back!

544
00:25:14,040 --> 00:25:15,560
Come on.

545
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:18,720
Hyph3n, hurry!

546
00:25:29,280 --> 00:25:31,120
Come on, come on.

547
00:25:31,160 --> 00:25:34,120
Kane, what happened? - It threw me.

548
00:25:34,160 --> 00:25:35,600
- Are you OK? - They've got Vorm!

549
00:25:37,240 --> 00:25:39,040
Get me back up there!

550
00:25:39,080 --> 00:25:40,800
You can't fight any more.

551
00:25:40,840 --> 00:25:42,040
Vorm needs me.

552
00:25:42,080 --> 00:25:44,960
We need you. You know this planet. Get us to the tunnels.

553
00:26:11,960 --> 00:26:14,160
How can it be even hotter down here?

554
00:26:14,200 --> 00:26:15,640
Oxygen check.

555
00:26:15,680 --> 00:26:17,600
Dad, we're doing oxygen checks.

556
00:26:17,640 --> 00:26:19,840
As green as the hair on our heads, Sylas.

557
00:26:19,880 --> 00:26:20,960
We're safe.

558
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:22,680
There's a short-range maintenance teleport here,

559
00:26:22,720 --> 00:26:24,480
which should just get us back to base.

560
00:26:24,520 --> 00:26:26,800
Stay close. There's only enough power for one use.

561
00:26:26,840 --> 00:26:30,160
Kane, when you were fighting the Dreg,

562
00:26:30,200 --> 00:26:32,000
did you see Benni?

563
00:26:32,040 --> 00:26:33,320
Yeah.

564
00:26:33,360 --> 00:26:35,080
Don't worry. I killed him.

565
00:26:35,120 --> 00:26:36,320
Oh!

566
00:26:36,360 --> 00:26:38,400
What did you just say?

567
00:26:38,440 --> 00:26:39,640
Benni?

568
00:26:39,680 --> 00:26:41,520
He asked me to.

569
00:26:41,560 --> 00:26:43,360
Oh!

570
00:26:43,400 --> 00:26:46,680
How...? How could you?!

571
00:26:46,720 --> 00:26:49,040
Come on. Come on, Vilma. I got you.

572
00:26:49,080 --> 00:26:51,240
What is wrong with you?

573
00:26:51,280 --> 00:26:53,040
Why didn't the Dreg kill him?

574
00:26:53,080 --> 00:26:54,320
He was having fun.

575
00:26:54,360 --> 00:26:56,280
There's a room down there where I stashed a medipack.

576
00:26:56,320 --> 00:26:58,880
Fetch it and we can get out of here.

577
00:26:58,920 --> 00:27:00,160
You're not getting out of anywhere.

578
00:27:00,200 --> 00:27:01,800
Bella!

579
00:27:01,840 --> 00:27:05,760
- What are you doing? - Shut up! I will shoot you.

580
00:27:07,760 --> 00:27:09,680
Where's the maintenance teleport, Kane?

581
00:27:09,720 --> 00:27:11,240
I'd rather die than tell you.

582
00:27:11,280 --> 00:27:12,680
Oh, you're going to die.

583
00:27:12,720 --> 00:27:14,600
It's just whether I shoot and kill you now

584
00:27:14,640 --> 00:27:16,240
or wound you and leave you to the Dregs.

585
00:27:16,280 --> 00:27:17,560
What is it you want?

586
00:27:17,600 --> 00:27:20,320
To burn everything you've built to the ground.

587
00:27:20,360 --> 00:27:21,640
Who are you?

588
00:27:22,840 --> 00:27:24,160
Me?

589
00:27:24,200 --> 00:27:25,440
Now I'm no-one.

590
00:27:25,480 --> 00:27:26,920
I was my dad's carer.

591
00:27:28,040 --> 00:27:31,760
Bella...why are you doing this?

592
00:27:31,800 --> 00:27:34,520
My mum didn't really die.

593
00:27:34,560 --> 00:27:37,480
She just never came to any of my birthdays.

594
00:27:37,520 --> 00:27:39,640
She didn't come to his funeral.

595
00:27:39,680 --> 00:27:42,400
And she doesn't even recognise me now.

596
00:27:44,280 --> 00:27:46,520
Trixabelle...

597
00:27:46,560 --> 00:27:49,160
Oh! And she gave me the name Trixabelle.

598
00:27:51,680 --> 00:27:53,720
The teleport's behind you.

599
00:27:56,480 --> 00:27:57,400
Oh!

600
00:27:57,440 --> 00:27:59,520
Come on!

601
00:28:00,840 --> 00:28:03,080
This is not the way to resolve a family dispute.

602
00:28:03,120 --> 00:28:06,280
How about good old-fashioned passive-aggressive discussion?

603
00:28:13,360 --> 00:28:15,160
Bella!

604
00:28:21,840 --> 00:28:23,480
Tranquillity Spa is experiencing...

605
00:28:23,520 --> 00:28:26,360
- I didn't ask you to do that! - You're welcome.

606
00:28:26,400 --> 00:28:28,040
We need to find a way to help the others get back.

607
00:28:28,080 --> 00:28:30,320
No. They can sort themselves out.

608
00:28:30,360 --> 00:28:33,040
Hey, hey, hey. These people are my family.

609
00:28:33,080 --> 00:28:35,400
We're finding a way.

610
00:28:35,440 --> 00:28:39,120
Too late. I'm here to burn this place down,

611
00:28:39,160 --> 00:28:42,400
and if you're not with me, you'll die here too.

612
00:28:42,440 --> 00:28:44,840
Our staff are aware. Relax.

613
00:28:47,440 --> 00:28:49,760
- Hang on, where's Ryan? - With Bella.

614
00:28:49,800 --> 00:28:51,600
Hopefully, the maintenance teleport

615
00:28:51,640 --> 00:28:52,720
has got them back to the hotel.

616
00:28:52,760 --> 00:28:55,920
OK, listen up. There's stairs just beyond here

617
00:28:55,960 --> 00:28:57,720
that will take us down and back.

618
00:28:57,760 --> 00:28:59,520
Just one catch - the route goes through a Dreg nest.

619
00:28:59,560 --> 00:29:02,120
That's madness! We'll never make it through!

620
00:29:05,040 --> 00:29:06,080
Oxygen supply falling.

621
00:29:06,120 --> 00:29:09,280
You talk too much. Using up all your oxygen.

622
00:29:09,320 --> 00:29:11,800
Consider urgently refilling this canister.

623
00:29:14,320 --> 00:29:17,400
Consider urgently refilling this canister.

624
00:29:19,520 --> 00:29:22,560
That daughter of yours, Kane - real chip off the old block.

625
00:29:22,600 --> 00:29:24,440
I didn't know she was here.

626
00:29:25,800 --> 00:29:28,920
So you left her and her dad and never got back in contact?

627
00:29:28,960 --> 00:29:31,160
You don't get to judge me.

628
00:29:31,200 --> 00:29:33,840
This project, Tranquillity Spa,

629
00:29:33,880 --> 00:29:36,440
I was only doing it to give to her.

630
00:29:37,840 --> 00:29:39,640
Maybe you should have mentioned that

631
00:29:39,680 --> 00:29:40,960
before you pulled a gun on her.

632
00:29:43,200 --> 00:29:45,760
OK, we're not really going to burn this place down,

633
00:29:45,800 --> 00:29:47,800
- are we? - Nope.

634
00:29:47,840 --> 00:29:49,600
We're blowing it up.

635
00:29:52,400 --> 00:29:53,400
What?

636
00:29:54,600 --> 00:29:56,720
You...built a bomb?

637
00:29:56,760 --> 00:29:59,640
Oh, I've built more than one.

638
00:30:07,640 --> 00:30:08,840
Reminder.

639
00:30:08,880 --> 00:30:11,680
Please locate breathable air in order to recharge supply.

640
00:30:11,720 --> 00:30:14,640
Oh, I'm sorry. I'm slowing you down.

641
00:30:14,680 --> 00:30:16,320
No, don't worry, don't worry.

642
00:30:18,200 --> 00:30:20,640
We're using too much oxygen.

643
00:30:23,640 --> 00:30:26,080
That's more of them. They know where we are.

644
00:30:26,120 --> 00:30:28,120
They'll be too fast for us. Take cover.

645
00:30:28,160 --> 00:30:29,960
I'll try and get a shot.

646
00:30:32,640 --> 00:30:35,240
What is it? Nothing. Keep moving.

647
00:30:35,280 --> 00:30:36,520
Hey, what are you doing?

648
00:30:36,560 --> 00:30:39,080
- I said it's nothing! - No, let us see!

649
00:30:45,520 --> 00:30:46,640
That looks like Russian.

650
00:30:49,840 --> 00:30:51,000
Novosibirsk.

651
00:30:52,120 --> 00:30:54,280
It's a Siberian underground station.

652
00:30:56,600 --> 00:30:58,000
This is Earth.

653
00:31:03,400 --> 00:31:06,680
No, no, no. It can't be Earth. This is nothing like Earth.

654
00:31:13,760 --> 00:31:15,800
Hide. Hide! Come on!

655
00:31:17,480 --> 00:31:18,760
Get down. I've got a shot.

656
00:31:18,800 --> 00:31:19,880
There's too many of them!

657
00:31:19,920 --> 00:31:22,000
You don't have enough ammunition!

658
00:31:22,040 --> 00:31:24,720
- We have to run for it. - Vilma can't run.

659
00:31:26,040 --> 00:31:30,600
Yaz, promise me...you'll run.

660
00:31:30,640 --> 00:31:32,000
You can't hide by yourself.

661
00:31:32,040 --> 00:31:34,240
Run.

662
00:31:34,280 --> 00:31:35,480
Stay alive.

663
00:31:36,720 --> 00:31:39,240
- Vilma! - Hey!

664
00:31:39,280 --> 00:31:41,000
- Over here!

665
00:31:41,040 --> 00:31:45,160
Which one of you hurt my Benni?!

666
00:31:48,640 --> 00:31:50,280
Don't tell me that's another hopper virus.

667
00:31:50,320 --> 00:31:51,920
Yep. And this time I'll put it somewhere

668
00:31:51,960 --> 00:31:53,680
the Doctor won't be able to isolate...

669
00:31:55,520 --> 00:31:57,080
You said you were with me!

670
00:31:57,120 --> 00:31:58,560
You can't blow this place up!

671
00:31:58,600 --> 00:32:01,040
I've spent my whole life wondering about her,

672
00:32:01,080 --> 00:32:03,560
and she's never thought once about me!

673
00:32:04,880 --> 00:32:06,520
I will shoot you.

674
00:32:06,560 --> 00:32:07,960
Tranquillity Spa is experiencing

675
00:32:08,000 --> 00:32:10,280
momentary operational difficulties.

676
00:32:10,320 --> 00:32:12,040
Go on, then.

677
00:32:14,440 --> 00:32:16,760
There was a smaller bomb in the bar too.

678
00:32:16,800 --> 00:32:18,760
I wasn't going to use it when anyone was here!

679
00:32:20,320 --> 00:32:22,280
But it just blew up the mainframe.

680
00:32:26,800 --> 00:32:29,480
This is a nest. Watch out for dormant Dregs.

681
00:32:29,520 --> 00:32:30,840
They sleep standing up.

682
00:32:30,880 --> 00:32:33,280
The stairs are the other side. We need to go through.

683
00:32:33,320 --> 00:32:34,680
Silently.

684
00:32:40,080 --> 00:32:42,480
We should have been able to help her.

685
00:32:42,520 --> 00:32:46,720
She died, bless her, so we can get out of here. Come on.

686
00:32:46,760 --> 00:32:48,640
- Tell us what you know.

687
00:32:48,680 --> 00:32:52,440
How can this be possible? How did the Dregs get here?

688
00:32:52,480 --> 00:32:54,040
When did the planet get invaded?

689
00:32:54,080 --> 00:32:56,400
Oxygen supply level 1%.

690
00:32:56,440 --> 00:32:58,840
You must find breathable air immediately.

691
00:32:58,880 --> 00:33:01,760
Oxygen supply level 1%.

692
00:33:01,800 --> 00:33:03,920
Immediate action required.

693
00:33:03,960 --> 00:33:06,240
Refill oxygen canister.

694
00:33:06,280 --> 00:33:08,200
Find breathable air.

695
00:33:08,240 --> 00:33:10,840
Failure to do so will result in threat to life.

696
00:33:18,920 --> 00:33:21,520
These stairs should take us back to Tranquillity.

697
00:33:24,720 --> 00:33:26,640
Wait, where's the Doc?

698
00:33:26,680 --> 00:33:28,640
Oxygen supply level 1%.

699
00:33:28,680 --> 00:33:31,720
You must find breathable air immediately.

700
00:33:31,760 --> 00:33:34,040
Oxygen supply level 1%.

701
00:33:34,080 --> 00:33:36,240
- Immediate action is required. - Oh, do shut up.

702
00:33:36,280 --> 00:33:38,680
- Refill oxygen canister.

703
00:33:38,720 --> 00:33:40,440
Find breathable air.

704
00:33:40,480 --> 00:33:43,440
Failure to do so will result in threat to life.

705
00:33:57,120 --> 00:33:59,520
Oxygen supply refilling.

706
00:33:59,560 --> 00:34:01,840
Oxygen supply refilling.

707
00:34:01,880 --> 00:34:04,480
Well, aren't you full of surprises?

708
00:34:04,520 --> 00:34:06,760
I need to understand one more thing now.

709
00:34:07,800 --> 00:34:09,840
Checking what's in here.

710
00:34:18,320 --> 00:34:20,560
That's what I was afraid of.

711
00:34:27,480 --> 00:34:29,040
Doctor!

712
00:34:32,800 --> 00:34:34,200
Over here!

713
00:34:34,240 --> 00:34:37,440
It's so strong without oxygen because it doesn't need it.

714
00:34:37,480 --> 00:34:40,240
It breathes carbon dioxide in and oxygen out,

715
00:34:40,280 --> 00:34:42,320
like a really angry tree!

716
00:34:42,360 --> 00:34:44,640
Thank you, but you should not have come back for me.

717
00:34:44,680 --> 00:34:45,960
I didn't.

718
00:34:46,000 --> 00:34:47,840
But I can buy you some time.

719
00:34:47,880 --> 00:34:50,000
- No. You owe her! - I owe you all.

720
00:34:50,040 --> 00:34:51,720
For starting this.

721
00:34:51,760 --> 00:34:53,000
Tell her I'm sorry.

722
00:34:54,240 --> 00:34:55,240
She deserved better.

723
00:34:57,160 --> 00:34:58,600
Kane!

724
00:34:59,680 --> 00:35:01,760
This is an emergency announcement...

725
00:35:01,800 --> 00:35:03,400
Whoa, what happened in here?

726
00:35:03,440 --> 00:35:04,600
I'm guessing Bella.

727
00:35:04,640 --> 00:35:05,840
If they think I'm clearing all this up...

728
00:35:08,280 --> 00:35:09,760
This is an emergency announcement.

729
00:35:09,800 --> 00:35:13,680
Come on. We need to close this up. Secure the room.

730
00:35:13,720 --> 00:35:14,960
Come on, give us a hand.

731
00:35:15,000 --> 00:35:17,400
One, two, three!

732
00:35:18,600 --> 00:35:20,040
We need to block this off.

733
00:35:20,080 --> 00:35:21,400
The vending machine! Come on.

734
00:35:21,440 --> 00:35:22,800
Good idea. Quick!

735
00:35:24,280 --> 00:35:25,720
Drop it, drop it! Come on, that's it.

736
00:35:25,760 --> 00:35:28,640
- Let's go, let's go!

737
00:35:28,680 --> 00:35:29,960
- Hey! Doctor! - Ryan!

738
00:35:30,000 --> 00:35:33,280
Bella, Sylas, Nevi, to the command centre now.

739
00:35:33,320 --> 00:35:35,680
We'll hold this off for as long as we can - somehow.

740
00:35:36,920 --> 00:35:38,440
"Made in China."

741
00:35:38,480 --> 00:35:39,960
Hey, how did this get here?

742
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:41,440
It never left.

743
00:35:41,480 --> 00:35:44,440
Orphan 55 - it's Earth. Your future.

744
00:35:46,640 --> 00:35:48,600
If this is Earth, then what are the Dregs?

745
00:35:48,640 --> 00:35:51,280
They're us. Mutated.

746
00:35:51,320 --> 00:35:53,600
Yes. The few that didn't die.

747
00:35:53,640 --> 00:35:55,000
Oh, no, they can't be.

748
00:35:55,040 --> 00:35:56,600
How did Earth end up like this?

749
00:35:56,640 --> 00:35:58,560
You had warnings from every scientist alive.

750
00:35:58,600 --> 00:36:00,320
- Global warming. - Huh?

751
00:36:00,360 --> 00:36:04,120
The food chain collapses. Mass migration. And war.

752
00:36:05,120 --> 00:36:06,560
I can't hold this much longer.

753
00:36:06,600 --> 00:36:08,080
We need to get out of here.

754
00:36:08,120 --> 00:36:09,880
When I say run...run.

755
00:36:09,920 --> 00:36:11,800
Run!

756
00:36:36,880 --> 00:36:39,520
Nevi, secure that door!

757
00:36:39,560 --> 00:36:41,240
I'm trying! The autolocks are playing up.

758
00:36:43,520 --> 00:36:45,120
Wait, where's Kane?

759
00:36:46,080 --> 00:36:48,160
She didn't make it back.

760
00:36:49,640 --> 00:36:51,560
Dad, you're doing it wrong.

761
00:36:51,600 --> 00:36:53,200
It needs a passkey to close it from the inside.

762
00:36:53,240 --> 00:36:56,640
Not now, Sylas, OK? I'm trying to concentrate.

763
00:36:56,680 --> 00:36:59,160
You never listen to me! Do it yourself, then!

764
00:36:59,200 --> 00:37:02,400
Doctor, look! Outside the dome.

765
00:37:04,080 --> 00:37:07,080
Dregs responding to the call.

766
00:37:07,120 --> 00:37:08,200
They're massing for an attack.

767
00:37:08,240 --> 00:37:10,680
And the ionic membrane's down, so they can all get in.

768
00:37:10,720 --> 00:37:11,840
We need to evacuate.

769
00:37:11,880 --> 00:37:14,120
We are on phantom power and the teleport is dead,

770
00:37:14,160 --> 00:37:15,920
but it still knows where each one of us came from.

771
00:37:15,960 --> 00:37:17,920
Nevi, you need to fix the teleport.

772
00:37:17,960 --> 00:37:18,960
No way, no, I'm...

773
00:37:19,000 --> 00:37:21,080
You're the only one who knows how to fix that thing.

774
00:37:21,120 --> 00:37:22,160
And if it doesn't work,

775
00:37:22,200 --> 00:37:23,960
we're all going to be stuck on this planet.

776
00:37:24,000 --> 00:37:25,800
The bounce capacitor is completely blown

777
00:37:25,840 --> 00:37:28,560
and the only fuel we've got left is syrillium 3,

778
00:37:28,600 --> 00:37:30,800
which isn't enough to get us off-planet.

779
00:37:30,840 --> 00:37:33,280
For that we need syrillium 4.

780
00:37:33,320 --> 00:37:37,360
Which is what...syrillium 3 mutates into

781
00:37:37,400 --> 00:37:39,920
when it's attacked by the hopper virus.

782
00:37:39,960 --> 00:37:43,080
- Good luck with that, Dad! - Autolocking linen cupboard.

783
00:37:45,600 --> 00:37:47,280
Open the door!

784
00:37:47,320 --> 00:37:49,920
Sylas is out there! I can't get the autolocks open!

785
00:37:49,960 --> 00:37:50,960
Where is he?!

786
00:37:51,000 --> 00:37:53,000
He's not in the corridor. He must have run.

787
00:37:53,040 --> 00:37:54,280
We're all going to die here.

788
00:37:54,320 --> 00:37:57,000
Not if I've got anything to do with it.

789
00:37:57,040 --> 00:37:58,840
I know how we can survive this.

790
00:37:58,880 --> 00:38:00,960
We have one advantage over them.

791
00:38:01,000 --> 00:38:03,360
Oxygen. We love it. The Dregs hate it.

792
00:38:03,400 --> 00:38:05,520
This whole dome is air-conditioned.

793
00:38:05,560 --> 00:38:08,720
If I can up the oxygen levels, the Dregs will be weakened

794
00:38:08,760 --> 00:38:10,440
and we'll get out of here. Now, Nevi...

795
00:38:10,480 --> 00:38:11,840
...get on it.

796
00:38:11,880 --> 00:38:14,440
Yaz, Ryan, the Dregs are going to attack

797
00:38:14,480 --> 00:38:17,200
the one place where the dome wall meets the hotel.

798
00:38:17,240 --> 00:38:18,400
The steam room.

799
00:38:18,440 --> 00:38:20,960
Keep them at bay and buy us as much time as you can.

800
00:38:21,000 --> 00:38:22,000
Graham, you're with Nevi.

801
00:38:22,040 --> 00:38:23,360
Bella, we're going to find Sylas.

802
00:38:23,400 --> 00:38:25,520
I'll try and boost the oxygen levels.

803
00:38:25,560 --> 00:38:27,440
Why should I take orders from you?

804
00:38:28,760 --> 00:38:30,000
You caused this mess.

805
00:38:30,040 --> 00:38:32,120
And now you're going to help fix it.

806
00:38:32,160 --> 00:38:34,400
Everyone regroup at the teleport.

807
00:38:34,440 --> 00:38:37,280
Now, I'm going to blitz these autolocks.

808
00:38:41,080 --> 00:38:43,320
OK. While I do this... - Yeah?

809
00:38:43,360 --> 00:38:46,480
...you open the drive core and isolate the syrillium 3.

810
00:38:46,520 --> 00:38:49,600
Are you having a laugh, mate? I'm... I'm a bus driver.

811
00:38:49,640 --> 00:38:51,280
We need to find something to barricade

812
00:38:51,320 --> 00:38:52,920
the breach in the wall, stop the Dregs getting in!

813
00:38:52,960 --> 00:38:54,120
Sun loungers?

814
00:38:54,160 --> 00:38:56,000
Yep, sun loungers. Last line of defence.

815
00:39:00,600 --> 00:39:03,040
Sylas must be here somewhere.

816
00:39:08,280 --> 00:39:10,040
Ha! Found him!

817
00:39:10,080 --> 00:39:12,440
One small problem...

818
00:39:12,480 --> 00:39:14,080
You've got a plan, right?

819
00:39:14,120 --> 00:39:15,840
Oh, it's brewing.

820
00:39:15,880 --> 00:39:19,000
At least three-eighths of a plan right here.

821
00:39:19,040 --> 00:39:20,520
Two-eighths.

822
00:39:20,560 --> 00:39:22,440
I'll be honest, all I've got is the letter P,

823
00:39:22,480 --> 00:39:24,160
but sometimes that's all I need.

824
00:39:34,840 --> 00:39:36,040
Hey, that's our oxygen supply!

825
00:39:36,080 --> 00:39:37,920
It's our only weapon!

826
00:39:41,960 --> 00:39:44,880
Got a plan. Sylas, stay there.

827
00:39:44,920 --> 00:39:45,920
I'll distract it.

828
00:39:45,960 --> 00:39:47,760
You grab Sylas and I'll meet you at the teleport.

829
00:39:47,800 --> 00:39:48,720
Oi!

830
00:39:48,760 --> 00:39:49,760
Wheezy!

831
00:39:49,800 --> 00:39:51,320
Over here!

832
00:39:51,360 --> 00:39:52,920
Yeah, I see you, Dreg leader,

833
00:39:52,960 --> 00:39:55,360
the alpha dog of the apex predators.

834
00:39:56,920 --> 00:39:59,360
Get to the teleport. It's OK.

835
00:40:00,920 --> 00:40:03,040
You call and your species responds.

836
00:40:04,760 --> 00:40:08,120
But we need to isolate you, and that CO2 has just shown me how.

837
00:40:08,160 --> 00:40:09,640
Right, change of plan.

838
00:40:09,680 --> 00:40:11,440
We need to keep it busy. Run!

839
00:40:12,560 --> 00:40:14,760
This way, Wheezy! Follow us!

840
00:40:14,800 --> 00:40:17,800
I can't do this! Where's my boy?

841
00:40:17,840 --> 00:40:18,920
He'd know what to do.

842
00:40:18,960 --> 00:40:20,880
Whoa, that's a mess.

843
00:40:24,600 --> 00:40:27,600
Graham, move over for a real mechanic.

844
00:40:27,640 --> 00:40:30,160
Gentlemen, let's make some syrillium 4.

845
00:40:34,760 --> 00:40:37,240
There's too many of them! There's nothing we can do!

846
00:40:37,280 --> 00:40:39,360
I've got an idea. Follow me!

847
00:40:40,520 --> 00:40:42,040
Get in the cage!

848
00:40:42,080 --> 00:40:44,160
What are you doing?

849
00:40:44,200 --> 00:40:46,880
Isolating Wheezy. It's the Dreg leader.

850
00:40:46,920 --> 00:40:48,680
Then why are we in the cage?

851
00:40:48,720 --> 00:40:50,640
Playing a hunch.

852
00:40:51,960 --> 00:40:53,960
First we weakened it with oxygen.

853
00:40:54,000 --> 00:40:57,360
Now we deny it the carbon dioxide it needs to breathe.

854
00:40:57,400 --> 00:41:00,040
I know you can hear me.

855
00:41:00,080 --> 00:41:01,480
I've been in your head.

856
00:41:01,520 --> 00:41:04,120
- This room is sealed.

857
00:41:04,160 --> 00:41:08,600
You need carbon dioxide to convert into oxygen

858
00:41:08,640 --> 00:41:10,600
so you can breathe.

859
00:41:10,640 --> 00:41:13,760
We need oxygen to make carbon dioxide.

860
00:41:13,800 --> 00:41:17,000
Right now we've got a perfect ecosystem.

861
00:41:17,040 --> 00:41:20,200
Kill us, and you die too.

862
00:41:20,240 --> 00:41:22,960
Sorry. This was a trap and you walked into it, Wheezy.

863
00:41:23,000 --> 00:41:25,040
- Step back.

864
00:41:25,080 --> 00:41:27,360
And let us out of that door.

865
00:41:27,400 --> 00:41:29,600
It's the only way you're gonna live.

866
00:41:32,520 --> 00:41:36,200
The people who used to have this planet could have changed,

867
00:41:36,240 --> 00:41:37,560
but they didn't,

868
00:41:37,600 --> 00:41:40,080
so they lost everything.

869
00:41:41,440 --> 00:41:44,920
Be smarter than what made you.

870
00:41:49,640 --> 00:41:51,120
Step away.

871
00:41:58,400 --> 00:42:00,120
Good Drag. Smart Dreg.

872
00:42:03,360 --> 00:42:04,720
Ready?

873
00:42:13,520 --> 00:42:16,440
The second you open that door, it's going to kill us.

874
00:42:16,480 --> 00:42:18,800
I'm not gonna open the door until it's in the cage.

875
00:42:18,840 --> 00:42:20,320
I'm hoping it understands that.

876
00:42:37,160 --> 00:42:39,000
Run. Run, run, run, run, run!

877
00:42:44,240 --> 00:42:45,880
You let Bella set this bomb?

878
00:42:45,920 --> 00:42:48,280
She had a lot of bombs and a gun.

879
00:42:48,320 --> 00:42:49,760
I wasn't gonna argue.

880
00:42:49,800 --> 00:42:51,880
Bella's got some serious issues.

881
00:42:51,920 --> 00:42:53,240
Yeah, lucky for us.

882
00:42:59,680 --> 00:43:00,800
This way.

883
00:43:04,280 --> 00:43:06,160
Add one hopper virus, leave to simmer,

884
00:43:06,200 --> 00:43:08,000
and we'll have our syrillium 4.

885
00:43:08,040 --> 00:43:11,440
- Well, hopefully. - Oh, Sylas! Well played, boys.

886
00:43:11,480 --> 00:43:12,520
Please wait.

887
00:43:12,560 --> 00:43:13,640
Teleport operations rebooting.

888
00:43:20,120 --> 00:43:22,400
Did you both forget to mention the massive bomb?!

889
00:43:22,440 --> 00:43:24,720
It's going to take about a minute to get to full power.

890
00:43:24,760 --> 00:43:26,000
Nevi, we don't have a minute.

891
00:43:26,040 --> 00:43:27,520
Teleport occupancy exceeded.

892
00:43:27,560 --> 00:43:30,120
There's too many people to transport.

893
00:43:31,960 --> 00:43:34,480
Teleport occupancy exceeded.

894
00:43:34,520 --> 00:43:36,760
- Get out of here. - No, Bella, come back here!

895
00:43:36,800 --> 00:43:39,800
This teleport is now fully operational.

896
00:43:39,840 --> 00:43:42,840
Nevi, I've set the system. You and Sylas can go.

897
00:43:42,880 --> 00:43:45,600
Sylas, you've been brilliant.

898
00:43:45,640 --> 00:43:47,160
Bye, Doctor.

899
00:43:54,280 --> 00:43:56,320
- Bella! Weapon failed on her!

900
00:43:58,160 --> 00:43:59,720
Get away from her!

901
00:44:09,640 --> 00:44:11,800
Got this.

902
00:44:15,000 --> 00:44:18,800
O'Brien, party of four. Return teleport profile located.

903
00:44:18,840 --> 00:44:19,920
Teleporting.

904
00:44:25,920 --> 00:44:27,840
We made it.

905
00:44:30,800 --> 00:44:32,840
She... She'll be OK.

906
00:44:32,880 --> 00:44:34,480
She'll be fine. She's with Kane.

907
00:44:34,520 --> 00:44:36,400
How are they going to be OK?

908
00:44:37,680 --> 00:44:39,080
No oxygen, no help.

909
00:44:40,800 --> 00:44:44,280
When did you know... that it was Earth?

910
00:44:45,960 --> 00:44:47,720
Just before you did.

911
00:44:53,720 --> 00:44:55,800
Look, I know what you're thinking.

912
00:44:55,840 --> 00:44:57,840
But it's one possible future.

913
00:44:57,880 --> 00:44:59,240
It's one timeline.

914
00:45:00,320 --> 00:45:03,320
You want me to tell you that Earth's going to be OK?

915
00:45:03,360 --> 00:45:04,680
Cos I can't.

916
00:45:05,960 --> 00:45:09,080
In your time, humanity is busy arguing over the washing-up

917
00:45:09,120 --> 00:45:11,160
while the house burns down.

918
00:45:11,200 --> 00:45:14,560
Unless people face facts and change,

919
00:45:14,600 --> 00:45:16,440
catastrophe is coming.

920
00:45:18,200 --> 00:45:19,720
But it's not decided.

921
00:45:21,160 --> 00:45:23,080
You know that.

922
00:45:23,120 --> 00:45:25,000
The future is not fixed.

923
00:45:25,040 --> 00:45:28,720
It depends on billions of decisions, and actions,

924
00:45:28,760 --> 00:45:31,080
and people stepping up.

925
00:45:32,360 --> 00:45:34,360
Humans.

926
00:45:34,400 --> 00:45:37,560
I think you forget how powerful you are.

927
00:45:37,600 --> 00:45:40,240
Lives change worlds.

928
00:45:40,280 --> 00:45:43,120
People can save planets, or wreck them.

929
00:45:43,160 --> 00:45:45,080
That's the choice.

930
00:45:45,120 --> 00:45:46,680
Be the best of humanity.

931
00:45:48,440 --> 00:45:49,680
Or...

932
00:46:26,880 --> 00:46:28,160
Gilded Age New York.

933
00:46:28,200 --> 00:46:30,560
This is when the modern world begins.

934
00:46:30,600 --> 00:46:31,760
It's only Nikola Tesla!

935
00:46:31,800 --> 00:46:34,400
The Niagara generator should be shut down.

1
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:45,640
งานดีมากพวกคุณ

2
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:47,320
- และขอโทษอีกครั้ง.

3
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:49,880
ฉันไม่รู้ว่ามันเป็นฤดูผสมพันธุ์ของพวกมัน

4
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:51,560
ใช่แล้วเกรแฮม ลูกชายของฉัน! ฉันได้มันแล้ว!

5
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:52,720
ได้อะไรมา?

6
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:54,800
คูปองใบที่ 6 จาก Bandohzi Herald

7
00:00:54,840 --> 00:00:56,400
เครื่องชงกาแฟชั้นบนส่งกาแฟมาให้ตลอดเลย

8
00:00:56,440 --> 00:00:57,440
หรืออยู่ชั้นล่าง?

9
00:00:57,480 --> 00:01:01,320
ยังไงก็เถอะ ไม่เป็นไรหรอก ฉันสังเกตเห็นว่าพวกเขามีข้อเสนออยู่

10
00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:03,960
สะสมคูปองครบ 6 ใบ รับสิทธิ์ท่องเที่ยวฟรี

11
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,280
ฉันอยากไปเที่ยวพักผ่อนฟรี

12
00:01:05,320 --> 00:01:07,760
- อยู่ที่ไหน? - สถานที่ที่เรียกว่า ความสงบ

13
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:09,360
ฉันก็เหมือนกัน ขอแค่มีแสงแดดเยอะๆ

14
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:11,800
และไม่มีปลาหมึกในอวกาศลึกอย่างแน่นอน

15
00:01:11,840 --> 00:01:13,280
อาจจะทำให้คุณออกจากอารมณ์รื่นเริงได้

16
00:01:14,320 --> 00:01:15,400
ฉันอารมณ์ดี

17
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:17,720
- นั่นคุณบอกแล้ว

18
00:01:17,760 --> 00:01:19,200
เดี๋ยวก่อน เกรแฮม พวกเขาไม่ได้

19
00:01:19,240 --> 00:01:20,400
หกสี่เหลี่ยมจัตุรัสสมบูรณ์ใช่ไหม?

20
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:22,200
อย่าเอาพวกมันมารวมกันก่อน!

21
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:24,080
สายเกินไปสำหรับเรื่องนั้น - เกิดอะไรขึ้น?

22
00:01:24,120 --> 00:01:26,120
หวังว่าคุณคงแพ็คของเรียบร้อยแล้วนะ ไม่ใช่แค่คูปองนะ

23
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:27,880
นั่นคือคิวบ์เทเลพอร์ต - เพิ่งเปิดใช้งาน

24
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:29,320
เรามีเวลาประมาณสี่วินาที

25
00:01:29,360 --> 00:01:31,280
ไม่ ไม่ ไม่ ไม่ ฉันต้องไปเอา Speedo ของฉันก่อน

26
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:35,280
ล้อเล่นนะ ใส่ไปแล้ว โฮ่โฮ่!

27
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:42,280
ยินดีต้อนรับสู่ทรานควิลลิตี้สปา

28
00:01:42,320 --> 00:01:44,920
โอ้ พวกคุณ! นี่มันโอเคนิดหน่อยใช่มั้ยล่ะ?

29
00:01:44,960 --> 00:01:45,960
ยินดีต้อนรับ!

30
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,800
โอไบรอัน ปาร์ตี้สี่คนเหรอ?

31
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:50,800
Bandohzi Herald มีคูปองอะไรบ้าง?

32
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:52,440
ฉันเป็น Hyph3n ที่มีเลข 3

33
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:55,760
เจ้าภาพลูกค้าของคุณที่ Tranquillity Spa

34
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:57,760
และผ่อนคลาย!

35
00:01:57,800 --> 00:01:59,160
สวัสดี Hyph3n เลข 3 หางสวยดีนะ

36
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:01,760
ฉันกังวลนิดหน่อยเรื่องการถูกแยกจากเรือของฉัน

37
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:04,360
ระบบของเราได้บันทึกตำแหน่งที่คุณมาไว้อย่างชัดเจน

38
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:06,880
คุณสามารถกลับมาได้ตลอดเวลา แต่คุณต้องจองไว้เป็นเวลาสองสัปดาห์

39
00:02:06,920 --> 00:02:08,320
รวมทุกอย่าง

40
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:09,360
เข้ามาได้เลย!

41
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:11,360
ห้องของคุณเพิ่งจะจัดเตรียมเสร็จ

42
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:12,800
ใช้เวลาสักครู่เพื่อสำรวจ

43
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:14,760
แล้วฉันจะมาหาคุณเมื่อพวกเขาพร้อม

44
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:16,240
ฉันจะไปหาสระน้ำ!

45
00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:18,000
ฉันกำลังดูว่าพวกเขามีอะไรอยู่ในอาคาร

46
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:21,200
แล้วฉันจะไปนั่งตรงนั้นสักสามชั่วโมง

47
00:02:21,240 --> 00:02:24,240
แล้วฉันจะลุกขึ้นไปนั่งที่อื่น

48
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:26,200
แล้วก็ค็อกเทล รวมทุกอย่างครับคุณหมอ

49
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:28,640
ต้องได้คูปองที่คุ้มค่า รีบจองเลย!

50
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:30,920
เอาล่ะ เกรแฮม ลูกชาย!

51
00:02:30,960 --> 00:02:32,880
แล้วฉันจะลองมองดูรอบๆ

52
00:02:32,920 --> 00:02:34,600
โดยตัวฉันเอง

53
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:45,240
สบายใจได้ครับ ทางทีมงานกำลังแจ้งให้ทราบครับ

54
00:02:47,320 --> 00:02:48,760
- ไวรัสระบบอื่น - ฟอร์ม ฉันไม่สนใจ

55
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:50,160
เราพบการละเมิดทางกายภาพ

56
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:51,600
มีคนเข้ามาแล้ว

57
00:02:51,640 --> 00:02:54,520
ค้นหา กักเก็บ และเผยแพร่ทางวิทยุ

58
00:02:54,560 --> 00:02:55,560
อย่าร่วมมือโดยปราศจากฉัน

59
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:05,800
ดูสิ วิลมา เชื่อไหมล่ะ

60
00:03:05,840 --> 00:03:08,520
โอ้ มันสมบูรณ์แบบนะ เบนนี่

61
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:10,160
ขอบคุณ

62
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:13,440
ฉันเห็นคู่บ่าวสาวบางคู่อยู่ที่แผนกต้อนรับ

63
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:15,400
สถานที่ที่ดีเยี่ยมสำหรับการมาฮันนีมูน

64
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:18,160
เรามีมา 46 ปีแล้ว

65
00:03:18,200 --> 00:03:19,960
เราไม่เคยจำเป็นต้องแต่งงาน

66
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:22,000
คุณบอกว่า...

67
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:23,080
...แต่...

68
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:24,440
ว้าว!

69
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:27,360
โอ้ สวัสดี ไม่เลวเลยใช่ไหมล่ะ?

70
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:29,000
มันสวยงามมากจริงๆ

71
00:03:29,040 --> 00:03:30,160
หนึ่ง...

72
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:31,520
ที่นี่มีครบทุกอย่าง

73
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:37,280
ยินดีต้อนรับสู่บาร์และโซนอาหารว่างของ Tranquillity

74
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:40,040
เราเสิร์ฟอาหารจานโปรดของคุณทุกอย่างแบบครบวงจร

75
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:41,520
โอ้ ของฟรี!

76
00:03:44,640 --> 00:03:46,040
- อู๋

77
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:47,840
- โอ๊ย! โอ๊ย!

78
00:03:47,880 --> 00:03:49,320
ทะเลาะกับตู้จำหน่ายสินค้าอัตโนมัติ?

79
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:51,000
ไม่หรอก มันแค่ทำให้ฉันโดนไฟฟ้าช็อต

80
00:03:51,040 --> 00:03:52,560
นั่นไม่ใช่เรื่องที่น่าตกใจ

81
